      "problem": "$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians to an equivalent measure in degrees. This gives\n\n$$\n(\\frac{\\pi }{3})(\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{\\pi })=\\frac{{180}^{∘}}{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since we know that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\sqrt{3},$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\operatorname{tan}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$",
